  "no_prevalence_gate": "Challenge prevalence is measured, not targeted. No acceptance loop for class balance. Metrics undefined on empty classes are null with reasons; binary comparison requires both classes and adequate negative support.",
  "protocol_version": "v4.challenge.protocol.1",
  "rationale": "200 independent Bernoulli observations have worst-case normal-approximation 95% half-width 1.96*sqrt(.25/200)=0.0693. This is only planning intuition; correlation worsens precision. Forty subjects, fifty episode/day clusters and twelve represented units guard concentration, not a claimed effective sample size. Each arm has twelve available unit clusters, so arm comparisons remain exploratory and uncertainty may be wide. Do not claim the original 300-row policy has been relaxed: these are new challenge objectives for a different estimand. If tighter original precision is required, this design is insufficient.",
  "support_failure": "Retain first complete draw, publish only predeclared aggregate support PASS/FAIL before freeze, preserve detailed counts privately. Do not regenerate, relax rules, drop families, add events or change seeds. Failed technical correctness blocks all evaluation. Failed support blocks a full-family adequacy claim and automatic progression to feature/model work; a separate user decision may permit an explicitly qualified protocol without changing data/targets. Actual counts and failed objectives are released in the final frozen evaluation report, or in a separately authorized retirement audit after ending use as independent evidence, never as tuning feedback.",
  "uncertainty_gate": "Support PASS alone does not establish adequate precision. If simultaneous family-recall interval width exceeds0.20, withhold a precise family conclusion even if counts pass; display estimate, counts and limitation. Arm/slice intervals require >=8 represented units; otherwise exploratory counts only."
